A27. Painful dental extractions. ~ FEES
A28. A slippery customer. ~ EEL
A29. Consumed at conventions besides time. (pl.) ~ NIPS
A30. A book the President reads on Sunday. ~ HYMN
A31. Kind of motives attributed to all politicians. ~ BASER
A33. Party of conventional elephants. ~ GOP
A34. A note seldom taken by bankers. ~ LA
A35. What pre-election promises don't lack. ~ LUSTRE
A36. Al says F.D.R.'s throwing it overboard. ~ DEMOCRACY
A37. These play political tunes. ~ ORGANS
A40. Cockeyed Kentuckians. ~ CK
A41. It takes a lot of these to buy a vote (sing.). ~ SOU
A43. The poor exceed the rich in these. ~ NEEDS
A44. What all parties are trying to get to first. ~ BASE
